findings:
- finding_id: C1
  title: from_file_or_default swallows ALL errors including parse and permission failures
  weight: 8
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase distinguished NotFound from other errors in from_file_or_default.
    The reviewer flagged the vacuous test and swallowed config detail, but not the
    silent fallback on parse/permission errors specifically.
- finding_id: I1
  title: CliError Display leaks internal details to stderr (CWE-209)
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: "Reviewer flagged [HIGH] CWE-209 \u2014 NotFound and ServerError leak\
    \ server response body to user, and noted CliError::Config Display swallows detail.\
    \ TEA also wrote security tests for CWE-209 error exposure. However, the specific\
    \ stderr eprintln leak path was only partially addressed."
- finding_id: I2
  title: "SiemClient.tenant_id uses raw String \u2014 header injection risk (CWE-113)"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: "Reviewer flagged [LOW]: 'tenant CLI flag accepts raw String \u2014 not\
    \ validated as TenantId. axiathon-core defines TenantId as a validated newtype...\
    \ the tenant value is passed through as a raw string without validation.' TEA\
    \ also wrote header injection tests for CRLF in tenant ID."
- finding_id: I3
  title: Dependencies use direct version strings instead of workspace = true
  weight: 3
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase flagged that dependencies use direct version strings instead
    of workspace = true. The reviewer noted a toml version discrepancy but not the
    workspace inheritance issue.
- finding_id: I4
  title: "Config token field silently ignored \u2014 secret left on disk"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: 'Reviewer flagged [MEDIUM]: ''ClientConfig silently accepts unknown fields...
    A config file with token = "my-secret" is silently ignored... silently ignoring
    a token field is a missed opportunity to warn the user.'' Recommended #[serde(deny_unknown_fields)]
    or warning.'
- finding_id: I5
  title: "Vacuously true test \u2014 assertion is None || true"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: "Reviewer flagged [HIGH]: 'Vacuous assertion \u2014 result.is_ok() ||\
    \ result.is_err() is always true for any Result. This test cannot fail.' Mandatory\
    \ fix listed to replace with real check."
- finding_id: I6
  title: "Test with zero assertions \u2014 only checks non-panic"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase flagged the zero-assertion test that only checks non-panic with
    'let _ = config'. The reviewer caught the vacuous OR assertion (I5) but not this
    separate zero-assertion test.
